/-!
# The original SL₃ block in the closure argument

The collapsed three-conjugate core proves that the original chosen L
is an SL₃(q)-block. Its model retains the actual quotient and conjugation
action. Natural H¹ gives S=V C_S(L), identifies C_S(L)=C_U(L), and proves
U=(U∩L)C_U(L), with the central supplement elementary abelian.

The assembled `Block.source_conclusions` supplies the special factor of
order q⁵, the elementary rank-4n quotient U/Z(U), and K-centralization
of Z(U). The actual quotient action and complete odd-extension
obstruction force K=L₁. The preceding natural-sum conclusion then gives
two natural copies on the literal U/V₁, U=O₂(K)=O₂(L₁)≤L, O₂(L)=V,
and T_L=(T∩L)C_T(L). It also identifies Z(U)=U′=Φ(U)=V₁ and the
special factor with U itself.

Only the authorized marked/core/collapse inputs, preceding Chapter 11
relative-component and flag conclusions, and 11.5.5(3)'s natural-sum
conclusion remain explicit. The parent closure argument supplies them
and retains the final outside-subgroup contradiction.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, 11.5.7, printed p.782.
-/
